IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Defence Force Retirement and Death Benefits (Pension Increases) Act 1974
-- (Cth). Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00163.txt.
-- Seat: the pensioner, widow or child.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Increase case 1974` IS ONE OF
    -- s 8
    `a DFRB pension under s 8`
    -- s 9
    `a DFRB s 82ZB pension under s 9`
    -- s 17
    `a DFRDB pension benefit under s 17`
    -- s 18
    `a DFRDB pension benefit under s 18`
    `a child's DFRB pension`

DECLARE `Pension 1974` HAS
    `CPI March 1974`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `CPI March 1973`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `AWE March 1974`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `AWE March 1973`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `case`                                              IS A `Increase case 1974`
    -- for a child's DFRDB pension, the additional pension (ss 17(2), 18(4))
    `annual amount before 1 July 1974`                  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 8(2)
    `annual amount before 1 July 1973`                  IS A NUMBER
    -- ss 9(2), 18(3): the first day of the counted period
    `period starts on`                                  IS A DATE

§ `Rules`

@ref s 3(3)
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to a tenth` x MEANS FLOOR (x TIMES 10 PLUS 1/2) DIVIDED BY 10

@ref s 3(1), (3)
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1974`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed percentage for` p MEANS
    `rounded to a tenth` (IF cpi AT MOST awe THEN cpi ELSE awe)
    WHERE
        cpi MEANS 14/10 TIMES (p's `CPI March 1974` MINUS p's `CPI March 1973`) TIMES 100 DIVIDED BY p's `CPI March 1973`
        awe MEANS (p's `AWE March 1974` MINUS p's `AWE March 1973`) TIMES 100 DIVIDED BY p's `AWE March 1973`

GIVEN s IS A DATE, k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`whole months from` s `counted` k MEANS
    IF `add months` s (k PLUS 1) AT MOST Date 1 7 1974
    THEN `whole months from` s `counted` (k PLUS 1)
    ELSE k

-- ss 9(2), (4)-(5), 18(3), (5)-(6)
@ref ss 9(2), (4)-(5), 18(3), (5)-(6)
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1974`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months for` p MEANS
    IF counted LESS THAN 1 THEN 1 ELSE counted
    WHERE
        start MEANS p's `period starts on`
        m MEANS `whole months from` start `counted` 0
        partStart MEANS `add months` start m
        partDays MEANS Day (Date 1 7 1974) MINUS Day partStart
        monthDays MEANS Day (`add months` start (m PLUS 1)) MINUS Day partStart
        counted MEANS IF partDays TIMES 2 AT LEAST monthDays AND partDays GREATER THAN 0 THEN m PLUS 1 ELSE m

@ref ss 7-9, 13, 16-18, 22
@export default The increase in my annual pension or pension benefit under the Defence Force Retirement and Death Benefits (Pension Increases) Act 1974 (Cth), from the pay-day of 4 July 1974, if both the CPI and average weekly earnings rose from March 1973 to March 1974: for an established DFRB pension, the prescribed percentage of the pension less 22.5% of its 1973 amount (s 8); for a recent s 82ZB pension, the prescribed percentage of 77.5% of it, scaled by months to 30 June 1974 over 12 (s 9); for a DFRDB pension benefit, the prescribed percentage of 71.43% of it (s 17), scaled likewise for a recent retirement or death (s 18). Nil for a child's DFRB pension. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1974`  @desc The index numbers, the case, the annual amounts, and the start of the counted period
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my 1974 increase for` p MEANS
    IF     NOT (p's `CPI March 1974` GREATER THAN p's `CPI March 1973`)
        OR NOT (p's `AWE March 1974` GREATER THAN p's `AWE March 1973`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE
        CONSIDER p's `case`
        WHEN `a child's DFRB pension` THEN 0
        WHEN `a DFRB pension under s 8` THEN
            pct DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES (p74 MINUS 225/1000 TIMES p's `annual amount before 1 July 1973`)
        WHEN `a DFRB s 82ZB pension under s 9` THEN
            IF late THEN 0 ELSE pct DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES 775/1000 TIMES p74 TIMES `the months for` p DIVIDED BY 12
        WHEN `a DFRDB pension benefit under s 17` THEN
            pct DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES 7143/10000 TIMES p74
        WHEN `a DFRDB pension benefit under s 18` THEN
            IF late THEN 0 ELSE pct DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES 7143/10000 TIMES p74 TIMES `the months for` p DIVIDED BY 12
    WHERE
        pct MEANS `the prescribed percentage for` p
        p74 MEANS p's `annual amount before 1 July 1974`
        -- ss 9(1), 18(1): "not being a pension (benefit) that became payable
        -- after 15 June 1974" (F5, changed after the independent pass)
        late MEANS p's `period starts on` GREATER THAN Date 15 6 1974
